  "title": "# Build: assistant-chat-mode (Opus, medium thinking; NO Fable on this account; keep it small) **Nam…",
  "asked": "# Build: assistant-chat-mode (Opus, medium thinking; NO Fable on this account; keep it small) **Name:** Assistant chat mode · **Category:** Feature ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"In the Claude in my app, it calls all kinds of tools. It takes forever. Why is it calling all these tools?\" (Amber: our rules make every Claude session check in first: claude_session_start, read Claude settings, post a session note, and some calls wait on approval countdowns. Offered a plain chat mode where it only uses tools when asked.) \"Yeah, build that right now.\" Target: the console's **AI assistant** (assistant@1, the chat Brett uses in the console web app) and **Gizmo** in AmberX (same backend, agent Gizmo). Book to a free named agent. Plan Studio plan for it. No new shared contracts (no Fable): add an optional field/setting only. ## Do 1. **Find why it's slow**: list every tool call the assistant makes on a plain 'hi' today (session start, agent pick, settings reads, session notes, memory, held/veto calls) with timings. Put it in the report. 2. **Chat mode (default ON for plain messages)**: a plain chat message gets a direct reply with **zero tool calls**: no claude_session_start, no settings read, no session note, no agent-pick prompt. Cache the agent/persona/settings once per conversation (refresh at most every 10 min) instead of per message. 3. **Tools only when asked**: tools turn on when the message asks for an action or live data (check/open/show/run/deploy/build/queue/status/find/add/etc., or a tool name). Plain-code intent check first (keyword/verb list, editable in settings), optional cheap model check second. Read-only tools never wait on veto countdowns in chat (they're allow-policy); anything that needs approval says so in one line. 4. **Toggle in the chat header**: Tools **Off / Auto (default) / On**, remembered per chat. Show a small 'used N tools' chip on replies that did use tools, expandable. 5. **Rules**: update shared RULES.md / CLAUDE.md / the assistant's MCP instructions with an explicit exemption: the console assistant and Gizmo in chat mode skip the session check-in rules. Build/headless sessions are unchanged. 6. Settings through the framework settings interface (default mode, intent words, cache time). Test: a plain 'hi' makes 0 tool calls and answers under ~3 s; 'check the build queue' still uses tools. Basic docs/README.md note, UI Review shot (non-blocking). 7. PR **through the merge queue only** (auto-land is OFF). Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
